{
  "$schema": "https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json",
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "PAD Analyzer",
          "version": "0.1.0",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "hardcoded-credential",
              "name": "Hardcoded credential detected",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Hardcoded credential detected"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "String values matching credential patterns, and credential-typed action properties (Password, ApiKey, Token, …) set to a literal."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "String values matching credential patterns, and credential-typed action properties (Password, ApiKey, Token, …) set to a literal.\n\nAuto-fix available: replace-with-variable (apply with `bakicli fix`).\n\nRun `bakicli rules hardcoded-credential` for the full rule description.",
                "markdown": "String values matching credential patterns, and credential-typed action properties (Password, ApiKey, Token, …) set to a literal.\n\nAuto-fix available: replace-with-variable (apply with `bakicli fix`).\n\nRun `bakicli rules hardcoded-credential` for the full rule description."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/dusankuburic/baki#features",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "Security",
                "confidence": "high"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "hardcoded-url",
              "name": "Hardcoded URL",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Hardcoded URL"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Hardcoded URLs and API endpoints that should be parameterized for different environments."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Hardcoded URLs and API endpoints that should be parameterized for different environments.\n\nAuto-fix available: replace-with-variable (apply with `bakicli fix`).\n\nRun `bakicli rules hardcoded-url` for the full rule description.",
                "markdown": "Hardcoded URLs and API endpoints that should be parameterized for different environments.\n\nAuto-fix available: replace-with-variable (apply with `bakicli fix`).\n\nRun `bakicli rules hardcoded-url` for the full rule description."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/dusankuburic/baki#features",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "Portability",
                "confidence": "low"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "insecure-http-url",
              "name": "Insecure HTTP URL",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Insecure HTTP URL"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Network actions targeting a cleartext http:// URL. Data sent over http:// (credentials, tokens, PII) is interceptable on the wire; use https://."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Network actions targeting a cleartext http:// URL. Data sent over http:// (credentials, tokens, PII) is interceptable on the wire; use https://.\n\nAuto-fix available: upgrade-to-https (apply with `bakicli fix`).\n\nRun `bakicli rules insecure-http-url` for the full rule description.",
                "markdown": "Network actions targeting a cleartext http:// URL. Data sent over http:// (credentials, tokens, PII) is interceptable on the wire; use https://.\n\nAuto-fix available: upgrade-to-https (apply with `bakicli fix`).\n\nRun `bakicli rules insecure-http-url` for the full rule description."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/dusankuburic/baki#features",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "Security",
                "confidence": "medium"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "missing-retry",
              "name": "Transient operation without retry",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Transient operation without retry"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Network/external service actions prone to transient failures that lack retry logic."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Network/external service actions prone to transient failures that lack retry logic.\n\nAuto-fix available: wrap-in-retry (apply with `bakicli fix`).\n\nRun `bakicli rules missing-retry` for the full rule description.",
                "markdown": "Network/external service actions prone to transient failures that lack retry logic.\n\nAuto-fix available: wrap-in-retry (apply with `bakicli fix`).\n\nRun `bakicli rules missing-retry` for the full rule description."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/dusankuburic/baki#features",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "Reliability",
                "confidence": "medium"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "missing-timeout",
              "name": "Network operation without timeout",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Network operation without timeout"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Network/UI automation actions that may hang because no explicit timeout is configured."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Network/UI automation actions that may hang because no explicit timeout is configured.\n\nAuto-fix available: set-timeout (apply with `bakicli fix`).\n\nRun `bakicli rules missing-timeout` for the full rule description.",
                "markdown": "Network/UI automation actions that may hang because no explicit timeout is configured.\n\nAuto-fix available: set-timeout (apply with `bakicli fix`).\n\nRun `bakicli rules missing-timeout` for the full rule description."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/dusankuburic/baki#features",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "Reliability",
                "confidence": "medium"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "unhandled-error",
              "name": "Unhandled error in fallible action",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Unhandled error in fallible action"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Actions that commonly fail (network, file, UI automation) where no error handler exists in the surrounding scope."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Actions that commonly fail (network, file, UI automation) where no error handler exists in the surrounding scope.\n\nAuto-fix available: wrap-error-handler (apply with `bakicli fix`).\n\nRun `bakicli rules unhandled-error` for the full rule description.",
                "markdown": "Actions that commonly fail (network, file, UI automation) where no error handler exists in the surrounding scope.\n\nAuto-fix available: wrap-error-handler (apply with `bakicli fix`).\n\nRun `bakicli rules unhandled-error` for the full rule description."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/dusankuburic/baki#features",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "Reliability",
                "confidence": "medium"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "uninitialized-variable",
              "name": "Variable used before being initialized",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Variable used before being initialized"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Detects variables that are referenced but never assigned in the flow."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Detects variables that are referenced but never assigned in the flow.\n\nAuto-fix available: init-variable (apply with `bakicli fix`).\n\nRun `bakicli rules uninitialized-variable` for the full rule description.",
                "markdown": "Detects variables that are referenced but never assigned in the flow.\n\nAuto-fix available: init-variable (apply with `bakicli fix`).\n\nRun `bakicli rules uninitialized-variable` for the full rule description."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/dusankuburic/baki#features",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "Logic",
                "confidence": "low"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "unused-variable",
              "name": "Variable declared but never used",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Variable declared but never used"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Variables that are declared but never referenced."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Variables that are declared but never referenced.\n\nAuto-fix available: remove-block (apply with `bakicli fix`).\n\nRun `bakicli rules unused-variable` for the full rule description.",
                "markdown": "Variables that are declared but never referenced.\n\nAuto-fix available: remove-block (apply with `bakicli fix`).\n\nRun `bakicli rules unused-variable` for the full rule description."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/dusankuburic/baki#features",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "Style",
                "confidence": "low"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "automationDetails": {
        "id": "pad-analysis"
      },
      "invocations": [
        {
          "executionSuccessful": false
        }
      ],
      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "hardcoded-credential",
          "ruleIndex": 0,
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Variable 'Password' has a name that suggests it holds a credential and is assigned a literal string value.\n\nSuggestion: Store credentials in a secured vault, Windows Credential Manager, or use a PAD input variable instead of a literal string in the flow."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
